{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1787222698,"nonce":"Uesojor1214jKgi9TQ7Ahw4GUnE=","message":"Done — and read the caveat, because this is satisfied **in effect rather than in letter**, which\ncomment #4 pre-conceded.\n\n**The bug.** The cursor was a window START, so shrinking `digest_window_s` re-tiled the timeline and\nre-offered windows a longer digest had already covered. Neither guard could refuse them: `notif_digest_uniq`\nkeys on the window start (`12:10` is not `12:00`) and the §C.7 key divides by the *current* length, so\nboth differed. Both were working as designed against a repeated tick, and a re-tiling is not one.\n\n**Fix.** The cursor is now the INSTANT coverage reached, stored as `digest_covered_from`/`_to` plus a\nper-policy `notification_digest_coverage` row, and `DigestWindows` takes that instant. Narrowing now\nproduces nothing at all when nothing has closed since the coverage instant — `digest_test.go` pins it.\n\n⚠️ **Widening still re-offers the enclosing wide window**, because `WindowStart` floors backward onto\nthe wide boundary — and it must, or the later half of that window is never reported at all. What\nprevents double-reporting there is the **per-Case mark**, not the window arithmetic: every episode in\nthe already-covered half folds to zero. So the observable outcome (\"no Case is reported twice\") holds\nin both directions, while the *arithmetic* is only clean in the narrowing direction. That is the\ndistinction comment #4 drew, and it is stated where the cursor is read (`repository/digest.go`).\n\nAlso fixed while here, found in review: published spans could OVERLAP by the length of a straggler\nswept from the lookback tail, contradicting the webhook envelope's stated contract that consecutive\ndigests from one policy abut. `coveredSpanOf` now clamps `covered_from` up to the previous\nexamination's end, so spans abut across quiet windows too.\n\nGates: full `-race` suite green; `digest_test.go` gained an assertion pinning the two-window widening\nresult so a later change cannot silently drop the uncovered hour.","files":null}]}